<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Strandzha</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Istranca Mountains</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Strandzha is a range of low, forested mountains in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> and the European part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>, rising to just over 1,000 metres. In antiquity it lay in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, and in 1903 it was the scene of the Preobrazhenie Uprising against Ottoman rule, which briefly set up the Strandzha Commune.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/strandzha.jpg" alt="Strandzha" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Strandzha-dinev-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
